ic\nL147: \nL148: [Input] About arXivLabs\nL149: # arXivLabs: experimental projects with community collaborators\nL150: \nL151: arXivLabs is a framework that allows collaborators to develop and share new arXiv features directly on our website.\nL152: \nL153: Both individuals and organizations that work with arXivLabs have embraced and accepted our values of openness, community, excellence, and user data privacy. arXiv is committed to these values and only works with partners that adhere to them.\nL154: Have an idea for a project that will add value for arXiv's community? cite43†Learn more about arXivLabs†info.arxiv.org .\nL155: \nL156: cite44†Which authors of this paper are endorsers? | Disable MathJax (cite45†What is MathJax?†info.arxiv.org )\nL157: \nL158: We gratefully acknowledge support from our major funders, cite46†member institutions†info.arxiv.org , , and all contributors.\nL159: cite47†About†info.arxiv.org · cite48†Help†info.arxiv.org · cite49†Contact†info.arxiv.org · cite50†Subscribe†info.arxiv.org · cite51†Copyright†info.arxiv.org · cite52†Privacy†info.arxiv.org · cite53†Accessibility†info.arxiv.org · cite54†Operational Status (opens in new tab)†status.arxiv.org L160: \nL161: Major funding support from\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[2511.15992v1] Detecting Sleeper Agents in Large Language Models via Semantic Drift Analysis (https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.15992v1)\nciteturn6582view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.15992v1\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 162\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Artificial Intelligence\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 20 Nov 2025]\nL9: # Title:Detecting Sleeper Agents in Large Language Models via Semantic Drift Analysis\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite5†Shahin Zanbaghi , cite6†Ryan Rostampour , cite7†Farhan Abid , cite8†Salim Al Jarmakani L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled Detecting Sleeper Agents in Large Language Models via Semantic Drift Analysis, by Shahin Zanbaghi and 3 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite9†View PDF cite10†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:Large Language Models (LLMs) can be backdoored to exhibit malicious behavior under specific deployment conditions while appearing safe during training a phenomenon known as \"sleeper agents.\" Recent work by Hubinger et al. demonstrated that these backdoors persist through safety training, yet no practical detection methods exist. We present a novel dual-method detection system combining semantic drift analysis with canary baseline comparison to identify backdoored LLMs in real-time.\nL17: Our approach uses Sentence-BERT embeddings to measure semantic deviation from safe baselines, complemented by injected canary questions that monitor response consistency. Evaluated on the official Cadenza-Labs dolphin-llama3-8B sleeper agent model, our system achieves 92.5% accuracy with 100% precision (zero false positives) and 85% recall.\nL18: The combined detection method operates in real-time (<1s per query), requires no model modification, and provides the first practical solution to LLM backdoor detection. Our work addresses a critical security gap in AI deployment and demonstrates that embedding-based detection can effectively identify deceptive model behavior without sacrificing deployment efficiency.\nL19: Comments:  | 7 pages, 3 figures, 1 table\nL20: Subjects:  | Artificial Intelligence (cs.AI)\nL21: MSC (Mathematical Subject Classification) classes:  | 68T50\nL22: ACM (Association of Computing Machinery Classification) classes:  | I.2.6; I.2.7; K.6.5\nL23: Cite as:  | cite11†arXiv:2511.15992 [cs.AI]\nL24:    | (or cite12†arXiv:2511.15992v1 [cs.AI] for this version)\nL25:    | cite13†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2511.15992†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL26: ## Submission history\nL27: \nL28: From: Shahin Zanbaghi [cite14†view email ]\nL29: [v1] Thu, 20 Nov 2025 02:42:41 UTC (1,061 KB)\nL30: \nL31: Full-text links:\nL32: \nL33: ## Access Paper:\nL34: \nL35: View a PDF of the paper titled Detecting Sleeper Agents in Large Language Models via Semantic Drift Analysis, by Shahin Zanbaghi and 3 other authors\nL36: \nL37:   * cite9†View PDF L38:   * cite10†HTML (experimental) L39:   * cite15†TeX Source L40: \nL41: cite16†view license†creativecommons.org L42: ### Current browse context:\nL43: \nL44: cs.AI\nL45: \nL46: cite17†< prev |   cite18†next > L47: \nL48: cite19†new | cite20†recent | cite21†2025-11 L49: \nL50: Change to browse by:\nL51: \nL52: cite22†cs L53: \nL54: ### References & Citations\nL55: \nL56:   * cite23†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L57:   * cite24†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L58:   * cite25†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org L59: \nL60: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL61: \nL62: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL63: \nL64: [Button: ×]\nL65: \nL66: loading...\nL67: \nL68: Data provided by:\nL69: \nL70: ### Bookmark\nL71: \nL72: [Input] Bibliographic Tools\nL73: # Bibliographic and Citation Tools\nL74: \nL75: [Input] Bibliographic Explorer Toggle\nL76: \nL77: Bibliographic Explorer (cite26†What is the Explorer?†info.arxiv.org )\nL78: \nL79: [Input] Connected Papers Toggle\nL80: \nL81: Connected Papers (cite27†What is Connected Papers?†www.connectedpapers.com )\nL82: \nL83: [Input] Litmaps Toggle\nL84: \nL85: Litmaps (cite28†What is Litmaps?†www.litmaps.co )\nL86: \nL87: [Input] scite.ai Toggle\nL88: \nL89: scite Smart Citations (cite29†What are Smart Citations?†www.scite.ai )\nL90: \nL91: [Input] Code, Data, Media\nL92: # Code, Data and Media Associated with this Article\nL93: \nL9